The native adaptation proves generic two-generator ideal congruence and
product factorization from actual ideal operations, together with the
image-unit criterion using an actual section, kernel, and checked unit
image. Checked field data supplies inverse witnesses; separate
constructions provide the rational and prime-residue field instances.

For the actual Weierstrass coordinate ring, it proves the opposite-point
ideal product identity with the curve equation, Jacobian partials,
nonsingularity branch, and field data visible in the hypotheses. The source
identity is Mathlib's XYIdeal_neg_mul. The native development supplies the
generator changes and unit arguments needed for that identity; it does not
assume the desired product theorem, an ideal inverse, or a class-group
result. Secant and tangent ideal products, fractional ideals, class groups,
and the full FLT proof remain outside this attribution's scope.
